# #1311: a lone operator overload must still type-check its argument. Before the fix a
# single-candidate `__or__` was accepted on arity alone, so this cell sailed through semantic
# analysis typed as `object` and died in codegen as SPY0908. It must be refused at semantic
# time as SPY0222 — never an internal error. `set | list` is an error in CPython too.
#
# This fixture used to pin two more cells, `set | frozenset` and `frozenset | set`, as deliberate
# refusals, and said in this header that #1312's implementation would update it when Sharpy
# adopted CPython's left-operand rule. That happened: both now WORK and are pinned by
# collections/set_frozenset_mixed_operators, whose values were checked against python3.
def main() -> None:
    s: set[int] = {1, 2}
    a = s | [3]
    print(a)
